<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name    "uncommander">
<!ENTITY version "2026.11.09a">
<!ENTITY plugdir "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/uncommander">
<!ENTITY cfgdir  "/boot/config/plugins/uncommander">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="hernandito" version="&version;" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hernandito/unCommander/main/uncommander.plg" min="6.12.0" icon="uncommander.png" launch="UnCommander" support="https://forums.unraid.net/topic/200949-plugin-uncommander-%E2%AD%90-a-powerful-two-pane-file-manager/">

<CHANGES>
###&version;
###2026.11.09a
The biggest update since the first release (full guide in the README on GitHub):
- Undo History: every change recorded, undo any step or part of one, days later
- Right-click menu, Copy/Cut/Paste, drag and drop, upload and download, the cart, Tag for delete, folder tree
- Archives open like folders (zip, 7z, rar, tar.*, iso): browse, view, play and copy out, read-only
- F-key layouts (Windows / Midnight Commander or your own), filter as you type, right-click ticks, hide the button bar, mark recent changes
- Colour themes (including Norton - an homage), Gallery view, picture editor, HEIC, video player with subtitles and GPU conversion
- Music library, tag editor (MusicBrainz), bottom player, playlists with Send to Plex/Kodi/Jellyfin/Navidrome/USB, Music check, Lidarr
- Built-in terminal with paste box, kept scrollback and auto-reconnect
- Tools: Duplicates, What's using space (updates after changes in the panes), Clean up, Fix access, User Scripts, Unassigned Devices mount/unmount; Tools button in the top bar
- Tabs and windows, own tab, iPad Home Screen app, Practice mode for new installs, fewer flash drive writes

###2026.10.18d
- First public release.
</CHANGES>

<!-- clean out an older build before laying down this one -->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
rm -rf &plugdir;
mkdir -p &plugdir; &cfgdir;
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/uncommander/README.md" Mode="0644">
<INLINE><![CDATA[**unCommander**

A two-pane, Midnight Commander-style file manager for unRAID. Browse two folders side by side and copy, move, rename, delete, compress, extract and compare files with the mouse, F-keys or taps on an iPad - with background jobs, Undo for every change, a restorable trash, batch rename, a viewer and editor, a picture editor, video and music players, playlists, a built-in terminal, and tools for duplicates, disk usage, empty folders, movie folders that lost their video (Radarr), TV shows with missing episodes (Sonarr) and music checks (Lidarr).
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>
